{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvaZTZUZ6zW6d1xgG7sf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**My recommendation: don't pick either option yet. Spend 1–2 weeks checking the evidence first, and agree up front what result means go.**\n\nThe signal so far is real but thin: three requests and one lost deal in a month. You already hold the data that would settle it, and checking it costs almost nothing next to £60k and six months.\n\n**Do this now:**\n\n1. **Go through the 140 lost deals.** Tag every loss that mentions security, compliance, SOC 2/ISO, questionnaires or procurement. Recorded loss reasons often hide the real one (\"went with a competitor\", \"no decision\"), so ask the sales reps about the larger deals.\n2. **Look at open deals as well.** Three requests in one month may be a new trend that last year's losses won't show. Count enterprise deals currently in the pipeline and how many have a security review coming.\n3. **Talk to the three prospects.** Would a SOC 2 Type I report, or a credible roadmap with a target date, keep the deal alive? Would they accept ISO 27001 instead? UK and EU buyers often prefer it.\n\n**Agree the go rule before you look at the data.** For example: if security-related losses plus at-risk pipeline, adjusted for win rate, are worth well over £60k plus about £20–30k a year for renewal audits, start now.\n\n**Either way:**\n- Write a security pack (policies, a standard questionnaire answered once, pen-test results) and put up a trust page. That costs little and helps whatever you decide.\n- If you go ahead, use a compliance automation tool and aim for Type I first. That gets you a report to show buyers sooner.\n\nThe deeper question for the CEO is whether enterprise is a deliberate target. If it is, SOC 2 is probably inevitable and the analysis mainly decides when. If not, one lost deal doesn't justify it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4596,"cache_read_input_tokens":3628,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4596},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"979a6cb2-ff38-4a94-908d-6be1f3f343d9","uuid":"46903614-573c-4445-a03a-0c5aef3d1249","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:07:13.056Z","request_id":"req_011CfvaZTKbf8oBV9oNzR1T6"}
